<p>E. THE SECRETARY She shall: 1. Write and keep all the minutes of the association, executive meetings and general assemblies in good English or French. 2. Draft all correspondences between the CWA Executive, assemblies and other organs and present them to the President for approval and signature. 3. Work in close collaboration with the President. 4. Keep all the updated records of enrolment into CWA of her area of jurisdiction and send a copy to the archives. 5. With the President, draw up the agenda for meetings. 6. Submit reports as may be required and share responsibility with the Vice Secretary.</p>
<p>F. THE VICE SECRETARY She shall: 1. Assist the Secretary in her functions. 2. Take over the duties of the Secretary when the latter is absent.</p>
<p>G. THE TREASURER She shall: 1. a) Receive from the Financial Secretary and immediately deposit in the appropriate diocesan account the money of the association. c) Present evidence at the next meeting of all transactions carried out since the last meeting. 2. Keep a strict and accurate account of all income and expenditure backed by the relevant receipts.</p>
<p>H. THE FINANCIAL SECRETARY She shall: 1. Request and collect the various dues required from members as well as other income for the association and immediately hand this over to the Treasurer against a receipt. 2. Keep a strict, accurate and up-to-date record of all the income of the association. 3. Give a financial statement at every meeting and render a written account quarterly. 4. Notify those who owe any dues of the association. 5. Work with the Treasurer to present a Balance Sheet annually and submit the records for auditing. 6. Help the various levels of the association to prepare budgets on an annual basis.</p>
<p>I. THE PUBLICITY SECRETARY She shall: 1. Initiate and publicise all the activities of CWA under the directives of the President and the Secretary. 2. Participate in the writing of the Newsletter as well as encourage members to contribute articles to the Newsletter. 3. At the General Level, be a member of the CWA Editorial Board.</p>
<p>J. SOCIAL SECRETARY She shall: 1. Organise or coordinate, following the general plan of the association, social days or evenings for the members of CWA. 2. Act as Discipline Mistress (Chief Whip) to ensure order and animation during meetings. 3. Organise the cleaning of meeting places and other places utilised by the association. 4. Act as Timekeeper.</p>
<p>K. THE ADVISERS They shall: 1. Advise at all levels on spiritual and moral issues (when need arises). 2. Advise on discipline, planning and organisation of special occasions and programmes.</p>
<p>L. AUDITORS They shall: 1. Control the management of CWA accounts, so that they are done following the basic rules of accounting. 2. Audit the records of the Treasurer and the Financial Secretary quarterly and whenever they deem it necessary without any prior notice. 3. Present at meetings, with the approval of the President, a reconciled statement of the Financial Secretary and Treasurer. 4. At the request of the executive, invite external auditors to audit the accounts of the association. M. CHAPLAINS They shall: 1. Be responsible for the planning and execution of the on-going Christian formation of members in collaboration with the executive. 2. Guide and foster the spiritual growth of CWA by providing spiritual enrichment to the life of the members at the respective levels. 3. Meet at least once every year with the General Chaplain to prepare the spiritual journey for the women for a coordinated spiritual direction.</p>
<p>N. THE ANIMATORS 1. They shall exist exclusively at Diocesan, Provincial and General Levels. 2. In accordance with the approved programme of the association they shall: a) Visit groups to inspire, give encouragement and coordinate their work. b) Organise and execute leadership courses, workshops, education and training courses (with the President and Executive). c) Have accurate records and statistics of all Branches, Zones, Divisions, and Dioceses to facilitate their work. d) Meet with the General Animators at least once a year to plan their work. e) Help the women to set up income-generating projects and follow up the technical part. f) Present a report to the Executive/association annually at their level of operation. 3. Animators who are not CWA members shall be Project/Social Managers.</p>
<p>O. LITURGIST Takes charge of all liturgical activities (Mass, prayers, dressing of the altar, etc.) under the supervision of the Chaplain.</p>
<p>P. ECUMENICAL REPRESENTATIVE She acts as a liaison person between CWA and all other ecumenical groups and in the organisation of all ecumenical activities within CWA.</p>',
