            'body' => '<p>MANAGEMENT OF FUNDS</p>
<p>1. a) At every level of the association, an enlarged executive shall meet to draw up the budget. b) The budget shall be presented at the general meeting of each level for adoption. 2. The preparation of these budgets shall cover the following subheadings: a) Dues b) Secretariat c) Documentation d) Communication e) Vocational Fund f) Transport g) Ordination/Final Profession h) Gifts (for the Diocesan, Provincial and General Levels only) i) International Contributions (for the General Executive only) j) Feeding k) Miscellaneous l) Depreciation m) Reserves, etc.</p>
<p>3. Social and charitable activities shall be first and foremost spiritually oriented; if any expenditure at all, it should be very minimal. 4. All gifts (in cash or kind) local or from abroad received in the name of the association shall be duly declared and used for the purpose for which they were solicited or simply offered. These should be duly acknowledged to the donors. 5. The Execution Commission shall comprise the following members: a) The President b) The Treasurer c) The Financial Secretary d) The Animator 6. The Execution Commission shall meet every three months to compare budget realisation and other financial reports. 7. The Execution Commission shall hold an evaluation meeting after every huge expenditure or event to reconcile financial statements. 8. The 7 October and 8 December special collections for the purposes of CWA shall remain at the Branch Level and be registered as part of the budget to be spent. The WUCWO Day of Prayer collection shall be forwarded to the General Fund for onward transmission. 9. Income at all levels shall be duly entered in the cash book and a receipt issued for all money received. 10. Expenses shall be approved at each level by the President, Treasurer and Financial Secretary, backed by authentic receipts, and duly entered in the cash book. 11. a) All profit realised from income generating projects shall be presented during executive and general meetings at the respective level. b) The Financial Secretary at every level shall prepare quarterly financial reports and present them to the Executive of her respective level, along with a statement of account from the financial institution in which the money of the level concerned is lodged, for study and appraisal. c) Where income generating projects exist, the Project Manager in collaboration with the Financial Secretary and Auditor(s) shall present quarterly and yearly project reports. Reports shall be backed by copies of necessary documents and shall be disseminated to all who have contributed towards the project. 12. a) Capital Investment shall be separated from all other income and expenditure. b) Depreciation shall be calculated on all fixed and moveable assets of the CWA, so that at any point in time the actual value of the assets shall be known. c) A reserves account shall be kept from the income realised, in order to build a good foundation for CWA Cameroon and for future use. 13. All assets of the CWA shall be codified, listed and presented to members during meetings at all levels. At the General Level, the assets shall be presented according to the various Dioceses. 14. All financial documents of the CWA shall be properly filed at all levels in order to preserve vital financial information and facilitate proper handing over. 15. The Auditors of the General Level shall audit the Provincial Level; the Auditors of the General and Provincial Levels shall audit the Diocesan Level; the Auditors of the Diocesan Level shall audit the Divisional Level; the Auditors of the Divisional Level shall audit the Zonal Level; and the Auditors of the Zonal Level shall audit the Branch Level once a year in the month of May. 16. An external, objective and independent audit firm shall be engaged to audit the accounts of the General Level once a year in the month of June. 17. The audit report(s) of each level shall be presented during executive and general meetings/conference/congress as the case may be.</p>',
        ],
        [
            'n' => 'IX',
            'title' => 'Electoral Officers',
            'body' => '<p>ELECTORAL OFFICERS 1. The Chaplain and other Priests and Religious present shall conduct the elections. 2. They shall be assisted by the Animator. 3. They can call upon some members of the association to assist them in the electoral process.</p>',
        ],
        [
            'n' => 'X',
            'title' => 'Elections',
            'body' => '<p>1. Elections shall only be held when there is a quorum of at least 2/3 of all the expected members at any given level. 2. For all the posts a simple majority of the votes cast shall be required. 3. For the levels where more than one Adviser and Auditor are needed, the first two names that have the highest votes would be considered voted into the executive. 4. To be eligible for elections at the different levels a member must have served the following lengths of time: a) At the Branch Level, 3 years except for newly created branches. b) At the Zonal Level, 5 years. c) At the Divisional Level, 7 years. d) At the Diocesan, Provincial and General Levels, at least 10 years, except for Dioceses that have existed for less than 10 years. 5. a) After elections there shall be an official handing over and the installation of the new executive within one (01) month in a special ceremony to be arranged at local level. b) All property of the association shall be handed over during the handing over ceremony.</p>',
        ],
        [
            'n' => 'XI',
            'title' => 'Voting Rights',
            'body' => '<p>1. At all levels voting rights shall be according to numerical strength and by those represented at congress (or general meeting) who have paid their dues. 2. At the General Level, for every 100 members of a Diocese there will be one voting right. If the remainder of the members is at least 50 members, an additional 01 vote would be allotted. 3. At the Provincial Level, for every 50 members of a Diocese there will be one voting right. If the remainder is at least 25 members, an additional 01 vote would be allotted. 4. At the Diocesan Level, for every 25 members of a Division, there will be one (01) voting right. If the remainder is at least 13 members, an additional 01 vote would be allotted. 5. At the Divisional Level, for every 15 members of a Zone there will be one (01) voting right. If the remainder is at least 08 members, an additional 01 vote would be allotted. 6. At the Zonal Level, for every 3 members of a Branch there will be one (01) voting right. 7. At the Branch Level, all members have voting rights. 8. In a case where there are many candidates, elections shall be done in two rounds. The first round shall select the first three candidates. Then the second round shall retain the one who has the highest number of votes cast. Otherwise, it shall be decided by a simple majority.</p>',
