            'n' => 'XIII',
            'title' => 'Uniform',
            'body' => '<p>1. The uniform shall be white polyester, short sleeve V-neck blouse without buttons or a zip, with "Maria wrappers" and a head-tie of the wrapper material, with white shoes, white beads (of a single layer), white earrings if these are to be worn, a black, white or CWA handbag and a white or navy blue pullover if it is to be worn, and a CWA Badge. 2. Although the uniform is paid for by the individual member, it remains the property of the association and shall be withdrawn by the Arbitration Committee from a member who fails to live up to its objectives. 3. Members shall wear the uniform during General, Provincial, Diocesan and Divisional meetings and on special occasions to be specified by the Diocesan Executive, e.g., religious occasions, ecumenical services, marriages of members and of their children. 4. The uniform shall also be worn during the funerals of members, of members\' husbands, parents, parents-in-law, children, brothers and sisters, and of the Clergy and Religious. 5. The CWA uniforms shall not be given to new members until their dedication into the association is accomplished. Therefore, uniforms can only be bought for members by Branch Presidents through the CWA Hierarchy. 6. Non-dedicated members shall wear the CWA blouse with a wrapper of blue or dark colour and a head-tie of the same wrapper material. 7. The Jubilee "Kaba" (social uniform) shall be worn at all social activities including wake-keeping. Members without the Jubilee "Kaba" shall wear a simply-designed "Kaba" of their choice with a blue headscarf.</p>',
