        [
            'n' => 'XIV',
            'title' => 'Emblem, Badge, Membership Card and Dedication',
            'body' => '<p>A. THE EMBLEM 1. The Emblem of the association shall be a cross in a circle with the abbreviation CWA in it, then the Greek letters A (Alpha) and Ω (Omega) and the dove with the peace plant in its beak and the gong, all these enclosed in a circle. 2. The symbols in the Emblem are: A (Alpha) which stands for Christ who is the beginning; Ω (Omega) which stands for Christ who is the end; The Dove with the peace plant stands for peace and hope; The Gong stands for the proclamation of the Good News; The Circle is a symbol of unity; The Cross is a symbol of salvation and Christ-like service.</p>
<p>A. CWA BADGE The CWA Badge shall be owned by each member and may be worn at all times.</p>
<p>B. MEMBERSHIP CARD 1. Every regular member shall own a membership card and pay her dues between 1 January and 31 March every year. 2. The membership card shall be designed to last for 5 years, with spaces for a passport-size photograph and signature. 3. A disabled member or one who is above 80 years of age and is unable to pay her dues shall benefit from all the privileges of the association.</p>
<p>C. CWA DAILY PRAYER/ANTHEM The CWA Daily Prayer shall be said and the Anthem sung in English or French before every meeting at all levels. The Anthem shall be sung at the Funeral Mass or burial of a member.</p>
<p>D. DEDICATION 1. Only members who have undergone the required probationary period of at least one year and who have passed the doctrinal formation test shall be admitted for dedication. 2. The preparation shall be followed up by the Chaplain, who will also administer the test. He can be assisted by a mandated CWA member(s). 3 The General Executive shall design Dedication and Transfer Certificates.</p>',
