        [
            'n' => 'XV',
            'title' => 'Sanctions',
            'body' => '<p>1. There shall be an Arbitration Committee at the Divisional and Zonal Levels comprising the following: a) Two responsible members of CWA chosen by the executive; b) Divisional or Zonal President; c) Divisional or Zonal Advisers; d) A Priest; e) Branch President. 2. Members at all levels of the association, who do not work in the spirit of CWA, shall be subject to advice and/or discipline, suspension or expulsion. 3. Members, who absent themselves from meetings for four (04) consecutive times without a reasonable excuse, shall be subject to a fine of 1 000 Francs CFA. After that, if there is no change, they shall be served warning letters; and if after three (03) months there is no change such members shall be expelled. 4. Members, who come late, disturb or leave meetings before time, shall be subject to advice and/or discipline with a fine of 50 to 100 Francs CFA. 5. Members, who are only "uniform members," shall be subject to advice and/or discipline. 6. Dioceses, which do not pay their dues completely by 31 March, may not: a) Propose candidates for General Elections; b) Vote or be voted for at congress; c) Propose amendments at congress. 7. In case the dues are not paid for two consecutive years, the Diocese concerned shall be considered to have withdrawn. 8. A Diocese that withdraws from CWA shall pay in all its debts before it is given back full rights into the association. 9. Only the General Executive has the right to publish or recommend any document for use in CWA or in the name of CWA. Any document found circulating within any of the structures of CWA (i.e., from Branch to Province) which is not from the appropriate authority will be immediately confiscated and the originator sanctioned together with the President of that level in which the document is being used.</p>',
