        [
            'n' => 'XVIII',
            'title' => 'Correspondence / Documentation',
            'body' => '<p>A. CORRESPONDENCE/DOCUMENTATION 1. Copies of incoming and outgoing correspondence to and from the General President shall be sent to the General Secretariat. 2. At general meetings a secretariat shall be set up, comprising two (02) secretaries from each Diocese under the supervision of the General Secretary. 3. Each Diocesan Secretary shall be responsible for collecting and distributing all documents for her Diocese. 4. There shall be no production or reproduction (photocopying) of any document of the association by a level without the written authorisation of the General Executive. 5. All correspondence to a higher organ must follow the association\'s hierarchy.</p>
<p>B. CWA OUTSIDE CAMEROON 1. For CWA structures outside Cameroon, the highest existing structure shall correspond directly with the General President. 2. CWA members visiting outside their country can attend CWA meetings in any Branch. They shall, however, not give any directives on any issue, e.g., dedication, Statutes/Bylaws, uniform, etc., except with a written permission from the General President.</p>',
